## 4. Fill in `databricks.yml`

Open `databricks.yml` and replace the TODO placeholders:

```yaml
targets:
  dev:
    workspace:
      host: https://<your-dev-workspace>.{{ if (eq .input_cloud `azure`) -}}azuredatabricks.net{{- else if (eq .input_cloud `aws`) -}}cloud.databricks.com{{- else -}}gcp.databricks.com{{- end }}
  staging:
    workspace:
      host: https://<your-staging-workspace>.{{ if (eq .input_cloud `azure`) -}}azuredatabricks.net{{- else if (eq .input_cloud `aws`) -}}cloud.databricks.com{{- else -}}gcp.databricks.com{{- end }}
  prod:
    workspace:
      host: https://<your-prod-workspace>.{{ if (eq .input_cloud `azure`) -}}azuredatabricks.net{{- else if (eq .input_cloud `aws`) -}}cloud.databricks.com{{- else -}}gcp.databricks.com{{- end }}
```

If you set up service principals in step 2c, update `run_as` for staging and prod:

```yaml
targets:
  staging:
    run_as:
      service_principal_name: <staging-sp-application-id>
  prod:
    run_as:
      service_principal_name: <prod-sp-application-id>
```

