## 5. CI/CD credentials

{{ if (or (eq .input_cicd_platform `github_actions`) (eq .input_cicd_platform `github_actions_for_github_enterprise_servers`)) -}}
### GitHub Actions

In the repository, go to **Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions** and add:

{{ if (eq .input_cloud `azure`) -}}
| Secret | Value |
|---|---|
| `STAGING_AZURE_SP_TENANT_ID` | Directory (tenant) ID of the staging app registration |
| `STAGING_AZURE_SP_APPLICATION_ID` | Application (client) ID of the staging app registration |
| `STAGING_AZURE_SP_CLIENT_SECRET` | Client secret value for the staging app |
| `PROD_AZURE_SP_TENANT_ID` | Tenant ID for the prod app registration |
| `PROD_AZURE_SP_APPLICATION_ID` | Application ID for the prod app registration |
| `PROD_AZURE_SP_CLIENT_SECRET` | Client secret value for the prod app |
{{ else -}}
| Secret | Value |
|---|---|
| `STAGING_WORKSPACE_TOKEN` | Personal access token (or M2M OAuth token) for the staging workspace's service principal |
| `PROD_WORKSPACE_TOKEN` | Personal access token (or M2M OAuth token) for the prod workspace's service principal |
{{- end }}

Under **Settings → Actions → General → Workflow permissions**, enable "Read and write permissions" so jobs can comment on PRs if you extend the workflows to do so.
{{ else if (eq .input_cicd_platform `gitlab`) -}}
### GitLab

In the project, go to **Settings → CI/CD → Variables** and add the following as **protected** variables (so they're only available to protected branches/tags):

{{ if (eq .input_cloud `azure`) -}}
| Variable | Value |
|---|---|
| `STAGING_AZURE_SP_TENANT_ID` | Directory (tenant) ID of the staging app registration |
| `STAGING_AZURE_SP_APPLICATION_ID` | Application (client) ID of the staging app registration |
| `STAGING_AZURE_SP_CLIENT_SECRET` | Client secret value for the staging app (mark masked) |
| `PROD_AZURE_SP_TENANT_ID` | Tenant ID for the prod app registration |
| `PROD_AZURE_SP_APPLICATION_ID` | Application ID for the prod app registration |
| `PROD_AZURE_SP_CLIENT_SECRET` | Client secret value for the prod app (mark masked) |
{{ else -}}
| Variable | Value |
|---|---|
| `STAGING_WORKSPACE_TOKEN` | PAT or OAuth token for the staging service principal (mark masked) |
| `PROD_WORKSPACE_TOKEN` | PAT or OAuth token for the prod service principal (mark masked) |
{{- end }}

In **Settings → CI/CD → General pipelines → CI/CD configuration file**, set the path to:

```
.gitlab/pipelines/{{ .input_project_name }}-triggers-cicd.yml
```

Under **Deployments → Environments**, create `staging` and `production` environments so pipelines can be approval-gated and the variables can scope to each environment.
{{ else if (eq .input_cicd_platform `azure_devops`) -}}
### Azure DevOps

1. Create a **variable group** named `{{ .input_root_dir }} variable group` under **Pipelines → Library**. Add the following variables:

   {{ if (eq .input_cloud `azure`) -}}
   | Variable | Value | Mark secret |
   |---|---|---|
   | `STAGING_AZURE_SP_TENANT_ID` | Directory (tenant) ID of the staging app registration | no |
   | `STAGING_AZURE_SP_APPLICATION_ID` | Application (client) ID of the staging app registration | no |
   | `STAGING_AZURE_SP_CLIENT_SECRET` | Client secret value for the staging app | yes |
   | `PROD_AZURE_SP_TENANT_ID` | Tenant ID for the prod app registration | no |
   | `PROD_AZURE_SP_APPLICATION_ID` | Application ID for the prod app registration | no |
   | `PROD_AZURE_SP_CLIENT_SECRET` | Client secret value for the prod app | yes |
   {{ else -}}
   | Variable | Value | Mark secret |
   |---|---|---|
   | `STAGING_WORKSPACE_TOKEN` | PAT or OAuth token for the staging service principal | yes |
   | `PROD_WORKSPACE_TOKEN` | PAT or OAuth token for the prod service principal | yes |
   {{- end }}

2. Create a **new pipeline** under **Pipelines → Pipelines → New pipeline → Azure Repos Git** → select this repo → **Existing Azure Pipelines YAML file** → pick `.azure/devops-pipelines/{{ .input_project_name }}-bundle-cicd.yml`.

3. Under the pipeline's settings, link it to the variable group from step 1.

4. Set a **branch policy** on `main` requiring the `BundleCI` stage to pass before merging PRs (Branches → main → Branch policies → Build validation).
{{- end }}

